The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
acrtc = to_amdgpu_crtc(wb_conn->encoder.crtc);
if (!acrtc) {
    DRM_ERROR("no amdgpu_crtc found\n");
    return;
}
afb = to_amdgpu_framebuffer(new_con_state->writeback_job->fb);
if (!afb) {
    DRM_ERROR("No amdgpu_framebuffer found\n");
    return;
}
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because if either `acrtc` or `afb` is not found (i.e., they are NULL), the function exits without freeing the allocated memory for `wb_info`, leading to a memory leak.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
	kfree(wb_info);
```
Reason:
These statements are added before the return statements when `acrtc` or `afb` is NULL, ensuring that the allocated memory for `wb_info` is properly deallocated, thus preventing the memory leak.

